# Data, API and scoring

Full schema in `docs/spec/03-data-model.md`. Stack adaptations in `docs/spec/ADAPTATIONS.md`
(Prisma instead of Drizzle; scoring lives in `lib/scoring/`).

## Schema rules

- Tenant-scoped engagement data uses `orgId` / `engagementId` with cascade deletes and indexes.
- Judgements that confirm human decisions must record who confirmed. AI must not write verdicts.
- Verdicts, phases, modes use string columns with Zod enums — not Postgres enums.
- Weights and statutory flags belong on criterion data, never hardcoded constants.
- Judgements and standard versions **supersede**; prefer history over silent overwrite.

## Migrations

- One logical change per migration, reversible where practical.
- Seeds are idempotent. GDS/Wales content is OGL v3.0 — attribution in exports.

## API / tRPC

- Zod-validate every input. Never trust an `engagementId` / `orgId` from the client body —
  inject from session context.
- Enforce role checks server-side.
- Evidence must link to at least one criterion (when that model lands).

## Scoring — `lib/scoring`

Pure, synchronous, no I/O. The only place an index or a verdict cap is computed.
Team Fit lives in `lib/scoring/fit.ts` and follows the same purity rule. Rigour signal *derivation*
thresholds come from `lib/playbook/keel.ts` (Delivery Playbook), not ad hoc constants in routers.

Rules (see `docs/spec/03-data-model.md`):

1. `index` is `null` when fewer than three criteria have a confirmed judgement.
2. Expired evidence cannot alone support `met`.
3. A broken chain caps the verdict at `at-risk` and reports `chainBreak`.
4. Statutory `not-met` sets low confidence and is reported separately.
5. Weights come from criterion data.
6. Deterministic. `now` is injected; no `Date.now()` inside scoring.

If a caller needs a number scoring doesn't return, extend `ScoringResult` — do not compute at the call site.
